---

This example demonstrates the local sensitivity contract. It does not simulate a cloud login. Real vault examples require the provider CLI, credentials and the configuration described in the manual; no provider access is needed here.

## Prerequisites

Use the complete repository checkout and start Mudflat as described in the [cookbook setup](https://github.com/weiqigod/curlew/blob/main/site/README.md). Run these commands from the repository root with `curlew` on PATH.

```bash
export MUDFLAT_URL="${MUDFLAT_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export MUDFLAT_WS_URL="${MUDFLAT_WS_URL:-ws://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export RUN_ID="cookbook-$(date +%s)-$$"
```

## Run it

```bash
curlew run examples/cookbook/secrets.yaml --var mud="$MUDFLAT_URL" --var ws="$MUDFLAT_WS_URL" --var run="$RUN_ID"
```

A successful execution exits 0. Read assertion outcomes as well as the exit code.
No example output or timing numbers are fabricated here.

## Complete collection

<!-- cookbook-source: examples/cookbook/secrets.yaml -->
```yaml
name: Local secret redaction
variables:
  demo_token:
    value: local-example-token
    sensitive: true
requests:
  - name: Echo a sensitive header
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "{{mud}}/echo"
      headers:
        Authorization: "Bearer {{demo_token}}"
    assertions:
      status: 200
```
